{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Peter at Work", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Choosing Peter for the Proposal", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Making and Responding to Suggestions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In the business world, at times, you have an idea, a recommendation or plan that you think could work for your company. It is important to use proper language to offer those ideas for someone to consider. Here is some language you can use for making and responding to recommendations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Making Suggestions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Responding to Suggestions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You might ... * <br/> You might want to ... *<br/> I would suggest ... *<br/> It's generally best/a good idea to ... *<br/> I'm thinking it might be a good idea to ... *<br/> I'd like to suggest/recommend ... *<br/> Why don't we ... ?</p>  * <span class=\\\"italic\\\">These expressions are followed by a bare infinitive (verb without \u2018to')</span></p>  In my experience, ... ** works really well.<br/> Have you tried ... ? **</p>  ** <span class=\\\"italic\\\">These expressions are followed by a noun or -ing form.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"That's not a bad idea.<br/>  I agree.<br/> I like the sound of that. <br/> That's a good idea. <br/> This sounds great. <br/> That would be great. <br/> I'll take it into consideration. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">More on \u201csuggest\u201d</span><br/>  It is important to remember that when \u2018suggest' and the verb that follows it have different subjects,  you use the pattern: \u201c<span class=\"italic\">suggest</span> + <span class=\"italic\">that</span> + <span class=\"italic\">someone</span> + <span class=\"italic\">should</span> + <span class=\"italic\">do something</span>\u201d ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">suggest that Peter should tell</span> Miranda that he is going to write the proposal.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'm thinking it might be a good idea to</span> have him write the proposal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I would suggest</span> you keep an eye on him if necessary.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">He might</span> need a little push to get work done.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Showing Flexibility", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In the workplace, it is important to show others that you are able to make changes or deal with situations that are constantly changing. You may need to adapt to different people and circumstances. It's an important trait in any employee and a vital quality. So here are some ways in which you can show flexibility.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Are you suggesting ... ? (+ -<span class=\"italic\">ing</span>)</li><li>Do you have any concerns? </li><li>All in good time. </li><li>If you say so. </li><li>I'm easy.</li> <li>Are you sure?</li><li>We might be jeopardizing ... . (+ <span class=\"italic\">noun</span>)</li><li>I'm open to ... (+ <span class=\"italic\">verb</span>)</li> <li>I'd be willing to ... (+ <span class=\"italic\">verb</span>)</li>  <li>I'm okay with ... </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Are you suggesting</span> asking Peter to do it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have some ideas, but <span class=\"strong\">I'm open to</span> suggestions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't think it's appropriate, but <span class=\"strong\">if you say so.</span>", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "keen", "type": "name"}, {"content": "wanting to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter is very keen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you can use to show flexibility.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "on the ball", "type": "name"}, {"content": "alert to new ideas or methods and quick to react", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Greta is on the ball.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "all in good time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in time with no risk of being late", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Everything will work out, all in good time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to count on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to rely or depend on someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There's too much counting on this proposal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "whatever it takes", "type": "name"}, {"content": "doing anything that is necessary in order to achieve a goal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to do whatever it takes to make sure the job is done.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to jeopardize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to risk harming or destroying something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think we'll be jeopardizing a critical opportunity.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "run the risk", "type": "name"}, {"content": "allowing the chance for harm or loss", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would never run the risk of ruining the business.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn6le14ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Work with a partner. Imagine that one of you is the manager of company. The other is the manager of a small department. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have a meeting to suggest some changes to the company. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember to use language necessary for making and accepting suggestions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I use language appropriate for a business meeting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make and accept suggestions in a meeting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about jobs and work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le14ob07re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le14ob07re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Hi Miranda. Have a seat. I must say I was impressed with your presentation. Thank you!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: It was fun to do. I think we all benefited.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Yes. Poor Ferdinand couldn't look at me when you discussed punctuality! He and Peter seemed to enjoy their scenario together. Speaking of Peter ... I'm thinking he might be a good candidate to write the proposal for Farmani.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Are you suggesting Peter Smith?"}, {"image": "engenn6le14ob07re2img06.jpg", "time": "28000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: I am. I'm thinking it might be a good idea to get him to do it. He's pretty keen.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: I agree.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Do you have any concerns?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: It's not a bad idea. It's just that, well, he struggles with deadlines. What do think about Greta?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: She's on the ball but lacks experience.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: True, but wouldn't you like to give her a chance?"}, {"image": "engenn6le14ob07re2img06.jpg", "time": "53000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: All in good time. Too much is counting on this proposal. Miranda, you didn't need me to refuse Peter time off now. You're too soft. You know, Peter will be inspired by this opportunity and do a good job but he might need a little boost to keep up his momentum. I think you could give him a scare now and then.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Like threaten his job?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Whatever it takes."}, {"image": "engenn6le14ob07re2img07.jpg", "time": "77500", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: I'll take it into consideration. Are you sure we might not be jeopardizing a critical opportunity?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: I would never run the risk. I would just suggest you take a firm approach with Peter when necessary. He can produce."}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le14ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le14ob07re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about jobs and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can make and respond to suggestions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can show flexibility.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What is the best way to respond to suggestions?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How can you show flexibility at work or school?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "There's a new opportunity at work. What is it?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Janet gives Peter more responsibility at work. Is she jeopardizing a <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">critical opportunity</span> or she is being <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_1\">too soft</span>?", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attem